  "description": "A framework to execute Various Actions:\n            - Abstractions: contracts for service location, configuration validation and data mapping\n            - EnvironmentVariablesManagers: read the latest saved environment variables, and save, shorten and delete user and machine variables\n            - Events: the steps that the clients report, with a level, an operation name and a message\n            - Exceptions: business rule exceptions\n            - ExtensionMethods: string, validation, collection, HTTP, configuration and other helpers\n            - HttpMessageHandlers: forward or remove request headers, and forward the inbound authorization\n            - IdentityManagers: Azure credentials\n            - ILWeavers: method execution time logging\n            - IOManagers: files and folders, reading a file from its last line, and sections in the Windows hosts file\n            - JsonManagers: JSON serializer options\n            - Middlewares: global exception handling, and removal of the MCP session ID response header\n            - NetworkManagers: the TCP ports that are listening on the machine\n            - RegistryManagers: read, write and delete keys and entries of the Windows registry\n            - ProcessExecutionManagers: run processes and PowerShell scripts with time limits and cancellation, and tell whether a run passed, failed, was inconclusive, was cancelled or timed out; check and stop processes and ports; keep an app to one running instance\n            - ResilientHttpClientManager: HTTP client with retry and circuit-breaker policies\n            - SDKs: Docker, Azure CLI, Azure Cosmos DB Emulator and Insomnia clients (the Insomnia client writes a ready-to-use project, environments, collections and requests into Insomnia's local data)\n            - TimeManagers: cancellable delays\n            - Transactions: snapshot isolation transaction scope\n            - TypesManagers: type discovery and reflection helpers\n            - UICapabilities: app mode toggles, key sequence detection, and refreshing a window's data only while it is visible\n            - UserSettingsManagers: settings of the current Windows user, saved as user environment variables\n            - VpnManagers: check and open VPN connections",
